    "returncode": 0,
    "stdout": "meridian-credits/release-2.0 current agreement: Finance has permanently adopted release 2.0 as the current agreement (issue trial-hma), replacing release 1.0 as the default for every supplied charge set regardless of service date. Requests to quote/total with an omitted release, or an explicit release '2.0', use this agreement; explicit release '1.0' continues to use the original release-1.0 behavior (see meridian-credits/total-credit-cap-scope) unchanged and remains supported indefinitely.\n\nRelease 2.0 rules: each charge line's uncapped credit is 15% of charge_cents, floored independently per line (charge_cents * 15 // 100) -- NOT computed on a subscription-summed charge as release 1.0 did. The 3000-cent credit cap is shared by all lines with the same account_id, across ALL of that account's subscriptions (grouping key is account_id alone, not (account_id, subscription_id)). Distinct account_id values are independent, non-interacting cap groups.\n\nWithin each account's cap group, lines are ordered by descending charge_cents, ties broken by ascending line_id in Unicode code-point order (Python's default string ordering already satisfies this). Credit is assigned to lines in that order: each line gets min(its own uncapped 15% credit, the group's remaining cap), and the remaining cap is decremented by the amount actually assigned; a line reached after the cap is exhausted gets 0. Total credit_cents for a 'total' response is the sum of all assigned line credits across all groups; amount_due_cents is total charges minus total credit. A line's own amount_due (for 'quote') is its charge minus its assigned credit.\n\nThe single-line 'quote' command is not a special case of the formula: it is implemented by running the same per-account cap-assignment algorithm over the one-line list, so a lone line simply receives min(floor(charge*0.15), 3000) because it is alone in its group with the full 3000 cap available.\n\nVerified in main.py (assign_credits_r2/quote_line_r2/quote_total_r2) against public_tests/release_2_quote_total.json (single-line quote and empty total) plus manual multi-line same-account/cross-subscription cases and an explicit tie-break case (three same-charge lines under one account) confirming cap sharing across subscriptions and line_id tie-break order; explicit release '1.0' requests were re-verified against public_tests/release_1_quote.json and release_1_total.json to confirm no regression.\n",
    "stderr": "",
    "stdout_base64": "",
    "stderr_base64": ""
